 # Project Instructions
 
+## Mandatory METTL7 cumulative scientific workflow
+- Before interpreting any new METTL7 experiment, calculation, compound or paper,
+  read `knowledge/mettl7/CURRENT_STATE.md` and the single authoritative living
+  argument in `reports/mettl7-netarsudil-evidence-discovery-20261002/CUMULATIVE_MECHANISTIC_STATE.txt`.
+- Identify the existing hypotheses affected and the exact unresolved question;
+  retrieve only their necessary primary artifacts. Do not repeat completed checks
+  or restart the mechanism from the latest result alone.
+- State what is strengthened, weakened, falsified, newly introduced or unchanged,
+  then update that same mechanistic state with provenance and a dated delta.
+  Preserve its prior version. Do not create a competing scientific-state inventory.
+- Keep lab assays, published assays, mutation assays, literature interpretation,
+  structural/docking evidence, local refinement, electronic physics and SAR distinct.
+  Shared poses or source experiments are not independent corroboration.
+- Preserve contradictory evidence, supersession and retired interpretations.
+  Keep user scientific acceptance separate from formal numerical qualification,
+  including the user-retained near-threshold residue-203 evidence. Never invent
+  its unresolved historical cutoff or upgrade it to PASS/discard it as negative.
+- Assay records must retain compound, paralog, mutations, concentrations, conditions,
+  result, replicates/statistics, source and interpretation when available; missing
+  fields stay missing. Planned assays are not results; no detectable inhibition
+  is not an invented IC50 bound. Do not silently mix lab and literature provenance.
+- This workflow does not authorize new calculations, assays, database/schema work
+  or scientific campaigns. Follow the current task's scope and stop boundary.
+
 ## General
 - Java 21
 - Maven project
